cause it started at case2 and accumulated the 3000ms gap. So for cooldown, the initial-gap issue doesn't matter because the cooling period starts after overheat is set, and the next call is after the full interval. For heating, the heater was already on during the interval before the call where overheat was false and heater_request true, but the timer didn't start until the call itself. That's the asymmetry: the heater enable condition was true before the call, but the timer only starts at the call. So the issue is that the heater enable condition was already true at the beginning of the interval, but the timer didn't know it.

